WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.452
Welcome to Tempo by ValueBridge: a productivity and time-management app that opens

2
00:00:05.452 --> 00:00:09.740
in your browser, works offline, and keeps your data on your own device.

3
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:16.075
This is your Today page. The capacity meter shows how much of your free working time

4
00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:20.898
is already planned, so you can spot an overbooked day before it happens. Below it:

5
00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:25.486
your timeline, your Big Three for the day, anything that needs attention, your

6
00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:27.133
habits, and your next alert.

7
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:33.764
Adding a task is as easy as typing a sentence. Tempo reads the date, the time, the

8
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:39.059
duration, the priority, the project, the energy level and the reminder as you type,

9
00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:42.823
and shows you what it understood. Press Enter, and it's in.

10
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:49.101
The Tasks page groups everything by when it's due. Or switch to the priority matrix

11
00:00:49.101 --> 00:00:52.503
to see what to do now, what to schedule, and what to drop.

12
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.939
Press Auto-plan, and Tempo fits your tasks into free time around your meetings, by

13
00:00:58.939 --> 00:01:03.916
deadline, priority and energy. Deep work goes into your peak hours and light work

14
00:01:03.916 --> 00:01:08.832
later, with a buffer around meetings and your lunch kept clear. Solid blocks are

15
00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:13.440
events, dashed blocks are task time, and you can drag any block to move it.

16
00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:19.200
While Tempo is open, alerts appear with a chime and a snooze button: before

17
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.091
meetings, before task blocks, a morning briefing, and a shutdown reminder at the end

18
00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:28.924
of the day. The alert centre shows what is coming up in the next twenty-four hours.

19
00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:35.254
The Focus timer runs timed work and break sessions linked to a task, logs the time

20
00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:40.054
against it, and keeps a parking lot for stray thoughts, so you can note them and

21
00:01:40.054 --> 00:01:40.594
carry on.

22
00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:46.672
Habits track streaks and weekly targets. Insights show your focus trend, your

23
00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:51.586
meeting load, and how your estimates compare with the time you log. Tempo can pad

24
00:01:51.586 --> 00:01:52.921
future plans to match.

25
00:01:55.268 --> 00:01:59.947
End each day with the shutdown checklist, and each week with the weekly review, to

26
00:01:59.947 --> 00:02:00.918
catch loose ends.

27
00:02:02.301 --> 00:02:07.802
In Settings, set your working hours, lunch, peak energy and alert preferences. Copy

28
00:02:07.802 --> 00:02:13.038
a backup whenever you like, or export your calendar to Google, Outlook or Apple

29
00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:16.551
Calendar. Support and licence details are under Help.

30
00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:22.404
Tempo opens on your phone too. Add it to your home screen and it opens like an app,

31
00:02:22.404 --> 00:02:25.634
with a one-day scheduler and in-app alerts while it is open.

32
00:02:27.034 --> 00:02:32.843
To get started: open the Tempo file, clear the example data, and set your working

33
00:02:32.843 --> 00:02:36.644
day. Then add your first task. Tempo, by ValueBridge.

